endobj
190 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (Instead of relying on average speeds, we focus on the 85th percentile to represent "free-flow" traffic. In traffic engineering, this value shows the speed that 85% of drivers naturally choose. If 85% of drivers are significantly exceeding the limit, it is a strong indicator that the map data is outdated or the sign is missing.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
191 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (Confidence Score Logic)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (The Confidence Score is our final metric for sign reliability, calculated by comparing the 85th percentile speed to the official speed limit. A high score \(near 100%\) confirms that drivers are following the map data, meaning the sign is likely correct. A low score indicates a major mismatch, suggesting the sign is either missing or incorrectly recorded in the database.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
